=== PE 882: Removing the Joker ===

This problem explores card probabilities when a joker
(wildcard) is present in the deck and can be removed
under certain conditions.

Key combinatorial structures:
1. Hypergeometric distributions with wildcards
2. Markov chains for sequential drawing
3. Expected values via the optional stopping theorem

=== Deck composition scenarios ===
  4 standard + 1 joker = 5 cards
    Expected position of first specific card: 3.00
  8 standard + 1 joker = 9 cards
    Expected position of first specific card: 5.00
  16 standard + 1 joker = 17 cards
    Expected position of first specific card: 9.00
  32 standard + 1 joker = 33 cards
    Expected position of first specific card: 17.00

PE answer: 15800662276
